ownerKey.created:
Your owner key's public half:
{key}

On the machine that runs binference, pass it to `binference init --owner-key-public`. Keep the code you wrote down offline; this machine keeps nothing.

webhook.created:
Alert rule {rule} waits for its card. Its URL, shown this once and kept nowhere:
{url}
Copy it into your alert now. Lost it? `binference webhook rotate {rule}` gives a new one.

webhook.rotated:
Alert rule {rule} has a new URL; the old one no longer works. Its URL, shown this once and kept nowhere:
{url}
Put it in your alert in place of the old one.
